@page "/about"
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "How this works"; }
<h1>How this works</h1>
<p>Each channel here is a Pkg channel served over HTTP, file for file as it is on the publisher's disk:
   an <code>index</code> with one line per version and CPU, and <code>objects/</code> with each version's
   manifest, its Ed25519 signature and its payload. Packages taken from a published archive, such as a
   nightly contrib build, list every file with its SHA-256 and point at the archive in <code>archives/</code>.</p>
<p>Pkg checks every manifest against the index, every signature against the manifest, and every file it
   installs against the manifest. The first install of a package pins the key that signed it, and a later
   version signed by another key is refused. The connection proves nothing and does not need to, which is
   why the same channels answer over plain http for machines without TLS.</p>
<h2>Publishing</h2>
<p>Publishers sign on their own machine; the portal never holds a signing key. A push sends what the
   portal lacks, and the portal publishes only what Pkg itself accepts: signatures, digests and the rule
   that a package keeps the key of its first version. A published version never changes and a push never
   removes one; its publisher can withdraw it.</p>
